CM_ BO_ 114 "0x072 - high-rate (100Hz) 7-byte message on bus 1. Non-standard counter position (not at byte 5 high). Unknown purpose.";
CM_ BO_ 120 "0x078 - chassis/body high-rate message on bus 1 (100Hz, 24B). Previously suspected to contain a turn signal bit (byte 4 bit 7) based on 2 brief ON episodes; redacted after proper 2-bit field search found the real turn signal on 0x58B instead. Byte 4 bit 7 is likely a different event flag. Counter at byte 8 HIGH nibble (not byte 5).";
CM_ BO_ 136 "0x088 - 100Hz 8B on bus 1. ACCEL_LIKE field (bytes 5-6) correlates +0.87 with longitudinal accel proxy. Scale 0.02 m/s^2 with offset -213.5 is a rough calibration based on session variance; re-calibrate against a known brake-to-stop event.";
CM_ BO_ 140 "0x08C - accelerator pedal @100Hz on bus 0. ACCEL_PEDAL is a 16-bit fraction scaled 100/65535 so 0..100% (observed max 96%). STEER_ANGLE_REQ (bytes 10-11) correlates +0.87 with 0x1AB.STEER_ANGLE via linear fit raw=10.14*steer+15487 (scale ~0.0986 deg/count). Residual std 53 deg suggests this is NOT a simple redundant angle readout - likely a steering angle REQUEST or CMD broadcast by a planning ECU (could be the LKA target angle when ADAS is engaged, or a pre-computed trajectory).";
CM_ BO_ 274 "0x112 - primary high-rate steering sensor on bus 1 (100Hz, 64B). Four independent 10-byte subframes each with CHECKSUM+COUNTER. STEER_ANGLE_1/_2 are 12-bit redundant readings centered at 2048 (offset -204.8, scale 0.1 deg). The former 'STEER_ANGLE_3' at bits 291|10 is actually LONG_ACCEL - correlation +0.94 with speed-derivative (longitudinal acceleration). BRAKE_PRESSED (byte 7 bit 1) and BRAKE_LIGHT (byte 7 bit 0) are the primary brake indicators at 100Hz (corr +0.77 and +0.41 with decel events). STEER_RATE is byte 8 alone (8 bits) - the previous 10-bit placement wrongly included the brake bits. Final 10 bytes (bytes 54..63) are full-entropy AUTOSAR SecOC or rolling session token.";
CM_ BO_ 303 "0x12F GEAR - 50Hz 12B bus 0. All 5 gear states validated via the dedicated gear-test drive 2026-04-17--13-23-29 and the Phase-5 gear-cycle in 2026-04-22. VAL table complete: 1=R, 2=N, 3=B, 8=D. PARK_ACTIVE=1 and GEAR_ENGAGED=0 when in P.";
CM_ BO_ 308 "0x134 - LKA CMD (validated 2026-04-21 across 1400+s of engagement). Byte 10 is TORQUE_CMD: always 0 unengaged, nonzero 3-5% of engaged frames during lane-drift corrections. Bytes 16-17 are a SecOC MAC (76-pair rolling code; NOT a control signal). Byte 17 high nibble is COUNTER - this is INTENTIONALLY within the MAC range (SecOC MAC is computed OVER the counter value). 0x134 does NOT follow the standard Renault CRC-at-byte-4 / counter-at-byte-5-high convention.";
CM_ BO_ 380 "0x17C EPS / driver torque sensor. DRIVER_TORQUE is biased-unsigned 16-bit centered at 32768 (offset -32768 → zero-centered signed). Observed mean ~0, std 63, range -731..+479 in driving log. Variance HIGHEST when LKAS_STATE=SUPPRESSED_BY_DRIVER (std 711 - driver actively turning); NARROWEST when LKAS_STATE=UNAVAILABLE (std 92). Matches Nissan 0x185 STEER_TORQUE_DRIVER pattern. EPS_MOTOR_POS (14-bit) tracks steering but with different phase than 0x1AB.STEER_ANGLE - likely motor-side resolver reading, not wheel angle.";
CM_ BO_ 403 "0x193 - 100Hz 16B on bus 1. Most bytes full-entropy, likely a continuous sensor stream. Has standard Renault counter at byte 5 high.";
CM_ BO_ 427 "0x1AB STEERING_CTRL - 100Hz 48B, 3 subframes (CRC at bytes 4/14/26, XOR 0x6A/0x17/0xCC). Sub A: LKAS_TORQUE_CMD (byte 7, 8-bit signed with offset -150, validated centred at 0 during LKAS active, constant 150 when LKAS UNAVAILABLE) + LKAS_STATE (byte 9 bits 1-2, 2-bit enum: 1=active/ready, 2=suppressed-by-driver, 3=unavailable; mirrors GWM/Nissan LKAS_STATE pattern). Sub B: STEER_ANGLE (16-bit 0.1 deg; invalid marker 3276.7 when 0xFFFF), STEER_TURN_CNT (16-bit rotation counter), STEER_RATE (16-bit signed 0.01 deg/s). Sub C: LKAS_UNK_27_28 (12-bit field, constant 2047 when LKAS unavailable, narrow 2857-3373 when active - NOT torque; semantic unclear, possibly a curvature/gain value) + UNK_C_BYTE30_31, UNK_C_BYTE32_33.";
CM_ BO_ 540 "0x21C - 50Hz 20B on bus 1. Candidate for redundant wheel-speed readout (same 20B/50Hz shape as 0x25F and 0x298).";
CM_ BO_ 554 "0x22A - vehicle-dynamics broadcast, 25Hz on bus 1 (64B). NOT an IMU: no field correlates with yaw (v*steer) > 0.2. Has four SPEED_LIKE_* fields that correlate 0.58-0.72 with vehicle speed (probably filtered/odometry speeds at different resolutions). Several 2-event state bits (byte 40, 56, 60) flipped at a few points in the drive - likely ACC/HDC/ESP state indicators. No standard Renault counter position.";
CM_ BO_ 600 "0x25F - 50Hz 20B on bus 1. Same layout as 0x21C and 0x298.";
CM_ BO_ 664 "0x298 - 50Hz 20B on bus 1. Same layout as 0x21C and 0x25F.";
CM_ BO_ 1310 "0x51E - 27Hz 8B on bus 1. Byte 1 has 187 unique values (high entropy).";
CM_ BO_ 843 "0x34B - ADAS object message (64B, 15Hz on bus 0). OBJ_A_VALID_OR_MOVING (byte 25 bit 2) and OBJ_B_VALID_OR_MOVING (byte 53 bit 2) were initially mis-identified as engagement flags - they're on 88% in the unengaged session too and only toggle with car motion state, not ADAS mode. Use 0x4B5.ADAS_ENGAGED instead for real engagement detection. The same bit at this position in each object record appears across the whole object-cluster (0x302..0x3DF) - synchronized.";
CM_ BO_ 847 "0x34F - ACC lead-vehicle target tracking. OBJ_A_PRESENT (byte 1) and OBJ_B_PRESENT (byte 29) take value 0xFF when no target and various low values when a target is tracked (the latter only happens during ADAS engagement). Two tracked objects per frame (bytes 0..27 and 28..55). OBJ_A_UNK_25_26 / OBJ_B_UNK_53_54 are strong candidates for target distance or relative position - during a 4s target-tracking window they correlated -0.99 with ego speed, BUT the same bytes also vary in the unengaged session so the interpretation is not yet confirmed.";
CM_ BO_ 1204 "0x4B4 - EPS/ADAS state on bus 1 (25Hz 8B). REFINED from 2026-04-22 stationary capture: byte 3 bit 7 is a HEARTBEAT that flips between 0/1 rapidly (XY <-> XY+0x80 alternation). The low 7 bits (EPS_STATE) encode the real state. During the stationary session observed 125+ unique values - a complex multi-state enum encoding several sub-fields. Value clusters: 0x40-0x58 (ACC-related states), 0x4F/0x5F (idle when engine on), 0x3D-0x3E (before ignition), 0xBE-0xCF (with heartbeat=1 variants). Full VAL_ table requires per-state controlled capture.";
CM_ BO_ 1205 "0x4B5 - PRIMARY ENGAGEMENT INDICATOR. Byte 0 (ADAS_ENGAGED) is 0 when ADAS is off and nonzero when armed/active. 30+ distinct values observed across sessions (range 0..138): driving-engaged 44-58, stationary ADAS-test 0-82 with fine 2-step granularity, pre-drive check 120-138, specific mode 124, peak 102 during a highway drive. State transitions are SEQUENCED (e.g. disengagement drops 100->98->94->88->84->78->72->68->62 in 2s), implying a packed state-level encoding not just a boolean. Full VAL_ table needs a controlled ADAS engagement-level test.";
CM_ BO_ 1419 "0x58B - RIGHT turn signal ONLY (10Hz 12B bus 0). Byte 11 bit 1 = TURN_SIGNAL_RIGHT. LEFT is NOT here - it is in 0x112.TURN_SIGNAL_LEFT (byte 14 bit 0) on bus 1. R5 splits the two directions across different messages (unusual; most OEMs pack L+R together). Confirmed over 33k R-blinker ON frames across 5+ driving sessions. Rare byte-11 values 0x82 (bits 1+7), 0x42 (bits 1+6), 0x22 (bits 1+5) appear <0.02% of the time and likely encode stalk-hold / lane-change-assist modifiers - needs more data to decode.";
CM_ BO_ 550 "Wheel speeds (3 subframes of 16 bytes, 50 Hz). Four wheel-speed signals (FL/FR/RL/RR) correlate 0.999+ with ego speed at scale 0.005 km/h — naming FL/FR/RL/RR is a guess; verify with a slip/turn test. UNK_SPEED_LIKE_A/B (bytes 10-11 / 32-33) were originally labeled VEHICLE_SPEED_A/B with scale 0.01 km/h, but they decode to 29.2 km/h when vehicle is stopped and ~60 km/h when actual speed is 40 — NOT clean km/h. Possibly motor-output speed or a gear-ratio-adjusted wheel speed. Use 0x3FA.VEHICLE_SPEED_KPH for the authoritative ego speed.";
CM_ BO_ 604 "4-byte 50 Hz message with only 2 active bytes. No room for a real checksum - DATA_A is just byte 0, not a CRC. COUNTER nibble at byte 1 bits 7..4.";
CM_ BO_ 853 "Opaque 25 Hz 64-byte stream appearing on both buses 0 and 1. Only header bits (1..3 of byte 3) show any structure - rest is full-entropy data. Likely camera/radar telemetry or CRC-protected proprietary payload.";
CM_ BO_ 1018 "Low-rate vehicle-speed + pedal echo on both buses. VEHICLE_SPEED_LOW_RES is a 6-bit field (0..63) - coarse; precise speed is on 0x226. ACCEL_PEDAL_LOW_RATE has scale 0.5 offset -18.5 matching user's original definition, observed 0..35% - may be a derived/smoothed signal rather than raw pedal.";
CM_ BO_ 1332 "BODY_534 - body-bus message on bus 1 (24 bytes). Note: the SAME address 0x534 also appears on bus 0 at 12 bytes - this entry describes ONLY the bus-1 variant.";
CM_ BO_ 1416 "Belts / doors / body state, 24 bytes, 2 subframes of 12 bytes. Each STATUS_* byte is a packed bitfield - decompose into individual booleans as you learn them.";
CM_ BO_ 1541 "Window control / window-state packet. Body bus, 1 Hz. Most payload is mostly-constant in normal driving.";
CM_ BO_ 1638 "0x666 - body bus @1Hz. BRAKE_PRESSED_LOW_RATE (byte 5 bit 3) corr +0.80 with decel proxy - secondary brake indicator, but too slow for realtime use. Primary brake is at 0x112 bit 57 (100Hz).";
CM_ BO_ 1661 "0x67D - MOTOR_RPM - drive motor speed. Raw 12-bit value 0..4095; observed 1986..2060 during a drive of 0..57 km/h (ratio ~37 at top speed matches an R5 E-Tech single-reduction ~9.3:1 gearbox with 195/55R16 tyres). Same address 0x67D also on bus 1, same 8-byte length, believed identical.";

CM_ SG_ 427 STEER_ANGLE "16-bit signed steering wheel angle, 0.1 deg. Raw 0xFFFF decodes to 3276.7 - this is the INVALID/UNAVAILABLE marker (EPS ECU has not yet initialized). Treat value 3276.7 as 'no reading' not a real angle.";
CM_ SG_ 303 GEAR_STATE "Gear enum (valid when GEAR_ENGAGED=1, PARK_ACTIVE=0): 1=R, 2=N, 3=B, 8=D. Validated across 149 segments with deliberate gear-test drive 2026-04-17--13-23-29.";
CM_ SG_ 303 PARK_ACTIVE "1 = car in Park. Mutually exclusive with GEAR_ENGAGED. When PARK_ACTIVE=1, GEAR_STATE is nominally 2 (unused during Park).";
CM_ SG_ 303 GEAR_ENGAGED "1 = a drive gear (R/N/B/D) is engaged. Inverse of PARK_ACTIVE across all 149 segments.";

VAL_ 303 GEAR_STATE 1 "R" 2 "N" 3 "B" 8 "D" ;
VAL_ 1100 GEAR_DIRECTION 1 "REVERSE" 2 "STATIONARY_PN" 3 "FORWARD_DB" ;
VAL_ 427 LKAS_STATE 1 "ACTIVE_OR_READY" 2 "SUPPRESSED_BY_DRIVER" 3 "UNAVAILABLE" ;
VAL_ 1233 FOLLOW_DISTANCE 0 "UNSET" 1 "NEAR" 2 "MID" 3 "FAR" ;
